  "provenance": {
    "label": "synthetic deployment-matrix mission diagnostic (features_only privacy)",
    "assets": "OpenAI-generated synthetic humans (owner-supplied); NOT real people, NOT real aerial data",
    "note": "results are integration/observability diagnostics, never real UAV, radio, or Jetson performance",
    "design": "model catalog: model_family x execution_mode, policy selects one config_id. Family deeplabv3_resnet50: onboard fp32, onboard fp16 (reduced precision via the torch kind's dtype knob; int8 needs TensorRT and stays out of scope), raw-RGB full offload (deliberately privacy-forbidden under this features_only contract), and TWO predefined-split tiers (pretrained_split kind): Entropic Student DeepLabV3-R50 beta 0.64 / 5.12 from the SC2 benchmark -- the split point is the SOURCE PAPER'S, adopted as a fixed catalog option, never searched or tuned here (provenance embedded per config). Family lraspp_mobilenet_v3_large: onboard fp32 / fp16 only -- no published split configuration for this architecture was found, and inventing one is forbidden, so the family honestly lacks a split tier. Wire payloads for pretrained_split are priced from the entropy-coded bitstream the head actually produces per frame (communication_mb_per_call is the nominal documentation value, measured on this world's frames at 512x384 input on CPU); head_latency_s, energy_j_per_call (head), and remote_compute_s are CONFIGURED mission-scale placeholders PENDING board measurement (the sc2 encoder is ~0.14M params). The checkpoints are local-only (gitignored cache), like the model-zoo weights. VOC-trained checkpoints on synthetic aerial markers are a documented domain mismatch (as in V2.1): this scenario exercises the catalog/accounting/privacy semantics, not attainable perception quality."
  },
